# The inner loop takes a guard as an argument: the test in front of it and the test at the end of each turn are about one object, so what they prove joins at its head.
# f0: the object is a value of the region, and it is live where the copy is entered from the region. There, and wherever the paths from there meet the others, it is joined with its copy and has
# a new name: in the copy the two tests would be about values with different names, and the read at the head of the inner loop about a third. So there is no copy.
# f1: the object comes from outside of the region and keeps its name
